  "interpretation": {
    "demonstrated": "All four attempted restoration boundaries match all 1200 saved fields exactly. Both same-object and new-object default reruns retain identical reported loss, total gradient norm, visit exposure, counters and all saved RNG states, but have small nonexact per-parameter gradients and resulting weights/moments.",
    "checkpoint_inference": "A new-object construction or disk-load state-loss explanation is not necessary: the same-object repeated restore already has 632 nonexact final fields. Together with the code audit and explicit unsupported deterministic backward, the evidence supports ordinary CUDA arithmetic nondeterminism. No missing saved model/EMA/Adam/RNG field has been demonstrated.",
    "limits": "This does not prove every unrecorded mutable runtime attribute is irrelevant, isolate the sole responsible kernel, guarantee long-run bitwise equivalence, or establish B2 learning quality. The unsupported-operator exception identifies a lack of deterministic implementation, not proof that this operator alone caused every observed difference.",
    "numerical_scale": "Largest absolute clipped-gradient discrepancy is 2.3283064365386963e-10. Largest model/EMA discrepancy is 7.450580596923828e-9 for same objects and 2.9802322387695312e-8 for new objects. No all-elements ULP bound was computed; large relative maxima near zero must be read with the absolute errors.",
    "unchanged_decision": "The original exact recovery gate remains failed; this probe also ends with a preserved unsupported-operation failure. Neither is retrospectively relabeled passed. This evidence does not falsify the B2 learning method, and does not itself adopt it.",
    "future_rule_proposal_not_implemented": "If B2 is used in a new explicitly registered candidate, keep exact pre-update checkpoint/model/EMA/Adam/RNG and exact deck/history/mask/exposure checks; distinguish these from floating post-update numerical equivalence. A separately named prospective recovery criterion could reuse the existing algorithm-comparison atol=rtol=2e-5, rather than fitting a new threshold to this maximum. Actual learning and throughput still require complete-cycle evidence.",
    "optional_pooling_followup_not_implemented": "For this fixed 18x32 to 6x8 spatial map, adaptive averaging has nonoverlapping 3x4 regions in real arithmetic. A separate avg_pool2d(kernel_size=(3,4),stride=(3,4)) study is possible, but changing CUDA reduction order needs its own forward/gradient acceptance. It is not required merely to rescue a bitwise diagnostic and no operator was changed.",
    "timing": "Per-arm update timings include synchronized CPU gradient copying. The first arm is cold; subsequent arms are warm. Restore, CPU snapshot and comparison times are reported separately. Three singleton updates cannot establish full-epoch throughput; strict arithmetic has no completed update timing.",
    "environment_difference": "All new probe arms have launcher CUBLAS_WORKSPACE_CONFIG=:4096:8 and synchronous gradient copies; the old failed gate had no such launcher setting. This is not a bitwise replay of the old gate process."
